# The right branch of Olmedo et al., TOPLAS 2018, Example 4.9 (p. 4:20): two fair coins (0 is
# heads), observing at least one head.  Three of the four runs pass, two of them with y = 0,
# so every normalisation gives 2/3; the program has no loop, so r2 (wp(S, f) / wp(S, 1)) is
# cwp here.
# Expected: valid.
nat x;
nat y;
{
	x := 0;
}[1/2]{
	x := 1;
}
{
	y := 0;
}[1/2]{
	y := 1;
}
observe(x = 0 || y = 0);
?Ex [[y = 0]] <= 0.7 r2
